            <ArticleTitle>Being reasonable during coronary revascularization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.26044</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The SYNTAX score is an angiographically based tool useful for clinical decision-making prior to coronary revascularization. The residual SYNTAX score (after angioplasty) is an independent predictor of clinical long-term outcome in patients with complex coronary artery disease. Both scores require functional lesion assessment. Adding clinical risk factors to both scores enhances their performance.</AbstractText>
